    <bpmn:process id="W_W281" name="W281. Self-Checkout (SCO) Exception &amp; Intervention Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer triggers a system exception at a self-checkout kiosk (e.g., weight mismatch, age-restricted item, voided item).
Frequency: Very High (Multiple times per hour)
Volume: Dozens per store per day
Owner: SCO Attendant
Participants: Customer, SCO Attendant, Loss Prevention
Source: workflow W281 — Self-Checkout (SCO) Exception &amp; Intervention Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W281_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W281_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W281_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W281_Lane3" name="SCO Attendant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W281_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W281_Start5" name="Customer triggers a system exception at a self-checkout kiosk (e.g., weight mismatch…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W281_Task6" name="Customer scans an item at the SCO kiosk; system detects an exception (weight…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer scans an item at the SCO kiosk; system detects an exception (weight mismatch in bagging area, age-restricted item, barcode duplication, or unexpected item removal)
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: —</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W281_Task7" name="SCO terminal locks the transaction, flashes an amber light above the kiosk, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SCO terminal locks the transaction, flashes an amber light above the kiosk, and displays a &quot;Please Wait for Assistance&quot; message
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): SCO Attendant
Duration: Real-time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W281_Task8" name="SCO Attendant receives a mobile alert on their handheld device detailing the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: SCO Attendant receives a mobile alert on their handheld device detailing the exception type, SKU, and kiosk number
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): SCO Attendant
Duration: &lt; 10 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W281_Task9" name="Attendant physically approaches the kiosk, verifies the customer and item…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Attendant physically approaches the kiosk, verifies the customer and item (checks ID for age-restricted items per RA 9211 §9 tobacco / PD 1619 volatile-solvent bans, verifies product match for weight mismatches), and scans their employee badge to unlock the terminal
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): SCO Supervisor
Duration: 30-60 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W281_Task10" name="Attendant clears the exception (approve, void item, or override price) and the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Attendant clears the exception (approve, void item, or override price) and the transaction resumes; if fraud suspected, Attendant discreetly alerts LP via mobile app
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 15-30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W281_Task11" name="System logs the override with: Attendant ID, exception type, SKU, timestamp…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System logs the override with: Attendant ID, exception type, SKU, timestamp, action taken, and kiosk number; feeds data to LP analytics dashboard (W37)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W281_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W281_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W281_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W281_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: SCO Attendant review and approval gate
Owner: SCO Attendant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W281_Assoc14" sourceRef="W281_Annotation13" targetRef="W281_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
