    <bpmn:process id="W_W516" name="W516. Self-Checkout (SCO) Daily Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store opening (SCO station activation) or customer approaches SCO station
Frequency: Daily during store operating hours
Volume: ~2 SCO stations per store × ~46 transactions/station/day = ~92 SCO transactions/store/day (~20% of the ~467 daily store transactions at stores with SCO); rolling out to 100 stores initially
Owner: SCO Attendant (dedicated role or Lead Cashier doubling)
Participants: SCO Attendant, Customer, Store Manager (escalation), Loss Prevention (analytics)
Source: workflow W516 — Self-Checkout (SCO) Daily Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W516_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W516_Lane1" name="SCO Attendant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W516_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W516_Lane3" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W516_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W516_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W516_Start6" name="Store opening (SCO station activation) or customer approaches SCO station">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W516_Task7" name="At store opening (W5A), SCO Attendant powers on SCO stations; system runs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: At store opening (W5A), SCO Attendant powers on SCO stations; system runs self-diagnostic (scanner, scale, payment terminal, receipt printer, coin dispenser); stations report &quot;Ready&quot; or flag hardware issues to IT Helpdesk (W48)
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task8" name="System loads daily price file, promotional rules, age-restricted SKU list, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System loads daily price file, promotional rules, age-restricted SKU list, and product master to SCO stations (same data set as staffed POS terminals per W5A.5)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task9" name="Customer initiates SCO session: scans first item; customer-facing screen…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer initiates SCO session: scans first item; customer-facing screen displays item name, price, and running total; system validates scanned barcode against product master
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task10" name="Weight verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Weight verification: after customer places scanned item in bagging area, system compares item weight against master weight tolerance (±5%); if mismatch: system pauses and alerts SCO Attendant with visual/audible signal
Responsible (R): System / SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): SCO Attendant
Duration: 15 sec if alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task11" name="Skip-scan detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Skip-scan detection: system monitors bagging area weight against cumulative expected weight of scanned items; if weight exceeds expected by tolerance threshold (indicating unscanned item in bagging area): system pauses transaction and alerts SCO Attendant
Responsible (R): System / SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): SCO Attendant
Duration: 15 sec if alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W516_Task12" name="If customer scans age-restricted SKU (per POS-029 age-restricted list): system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: If customer scans age-restricted SKU (per POS-029 age-restricted list): system pauses transaction; SCO Attendant approaches customer, requests government-issued photo ID, verifies age on SCO Attendant terminal (separate from SCO customer screen); SCO Attendant enters approval or denial on Attendant terminal — customer screen shows &quot;Age verification in progress&quot;; if denied: system removes item from transaction and displays denial message per W520
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): SCO Attendant
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task13" name="Customer completes scanning all items; system displays total with promotional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer completes scanning all items; system displays total with promotional pricing auto-applied (same promo engine as W5B.6); customer selects payment method on screen
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task14" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Payment processing: cash — system accepts bills/coins via cash recycler, calculates and dispenses change; card — customer inserts/taps on PIN pad, payment processed per standard card integration (W5B.7); e-wallet — customer scans QR code on SCO screen or taps phone on NFC reader; split tender — customer selects &quot;Split Payment&quot; and chooses tender combination
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–90 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W516_Task15" name="System prints receipt; offers e-receipt option per W528; customer collects…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: System prints receipt; offers e-receipt option per W528; customer collects receipt and bags
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W516_Task16" name="Exception / intervention escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Exception / intervention escalation: if SCO station encounters any unresolvable exception (coupon validation failure, loyalty card read error, catch-weight item, trade account pricing, void request, price dispute, suspected fraudulent scanning): SCO Attendant converts SCO transaction to assisted checkout at the SCO station or redirects customer to nearest staffed POS terminal; SCO Attendant can recall SCO transaction on their terminal and complete as assisted checkout per W5B
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–5 min per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W516_Task17" name="At store closing (W5F), SCO Attendant closes SCO stations: system generates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: At store closing (W5F), SCO Attendant closes SCO stations: system generates SCO-specific Z-report (transaction count, revenue by tender, void count, exception count, weight-alert count); SCO Attendant reconciles cash recycler contents against Z-report; secures cash per W5F.5–5b standard procedures
Responsible (R): SCO Attendant
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W516_Task18" name="Weekly: Store Manager reviews SCO analytics dashboard — SCO transaction volume…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Weekly: Store Manager reviews SCO analytics dashboard — SCO transaction volume as % of total store throughput, SCO exception rate, SCO void rate, weight-alert frequency, skip-scan alert frequency, average SCO transaction time vs. staffed POS, SCO customer satisfaction (from receipt QR survey W65); identifies SCO stations or stores with high exception rates for LP review or retraining
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W516_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W516_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W516_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W516_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: SCO Attendant (dedicated role or Lead Cashier doubling) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: SCO Attendant (dedicated role or Lead Cashier doubling)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W516_Assoc21" sourceRef="W516_Annotation20" targetRef="W516_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W516_Flow22" sourceRef="W516_Start6" targetRef="W516_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W516_Flow23" sourceRef="W516_Task7" targetRef="W516_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W516_Flow24" sourceRef="W516_Task8" targetRef="W516_Task9" />
