    <bpmn:process id="W_W521" name="W521. POS Transaction Suspend, Park &amp; Recall" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cashier needs to pause a transaction mid-sale (customer forgot wallet, needs price check, returns to floor for another item, customer asks to add gift wrapping, queue management)
Frequency: Multiple daily per store — estimated 5–15 suspensions per store per day
Volume: ~1,000–3,000 suspended transactions/day chain-wide
Owner: Cashier
Participants: Cashier, Customer, Store Manager (override for cross-terminal recall)
Source: workflow W521 — POS Transaction Suspend, Park &amp; Recall</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W521_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W521_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W521_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W521_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W521_Start4" name="Cashier needs to pause a transaction mid-sale (customer forgot wallet, needs price check…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W521_Task5" name="Mid-transaction, Cashier or Customer identifies need to suspend: customer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Mid-transaction, Cashier or Customer identifies need to suspend: customer forgot payment method, wants to get another item, requests price check, or customer needs assistance (elderly, bulky item carry)
Responsible (R): Cashier / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: —</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W521_Task6" name="Cashier selects &quot;Suspend Transaction&quot; on POS; system prompts for reason code…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cashier selects &quot;Suspend Transaction&quot; on POS; system prompts for reason code (Customer Forgot Payment / Customer Returning to Floor / Price Check Needed / Customer Needs Assistance / Other); Cashier selects reason code
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task7" name="System generates unique suspend ID (displayed on cashier screen and printed on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System generates unique suspend ID (displayed on cashier screen and printed on suspend slip); system parks transaction in suspended transaction queue; all scanned items, applied promotions, and customer loyalty (if scanned) are preserved
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task8" name="System temporarily locks cash drawer — no other transaction can start on this…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System temporarily locks cash drawer — no other transaction can start on this terminal until suspended transaction is recalled OR Cashier explicitly starts a new transaction (new transaction clears the suspend lock)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task9" name="Cashier prints suspend slip (small receipt with suspend ID, item count, running…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cashier prints suspend slip (small receipt with suspend ID, item count, running total, and reason code); hands to customer or keeps at terminal
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W521_Task10" name="Customer returns to same terminal; Cashier selects &quot;Recall Suspended&quot; and scans…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer returns to same terminal; Cashier selects &quot;Recall Suspended&quot; and scans or enters suspend ID (or selects from suspended transaction list on screen); system restores all items, promotions, and loyalty data; transaction resumes from point of suspension
Responsible (R): Cashier / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W521_Task11" name="different terminal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If customer returns to a different terminal: original Cashier&#x27;s suspended transaction is visible on all terminals at the store; any Cashier at any terminal can recall by entering suspend ID; however, if payment-related data was partially entered (e.g., partial card swipe), system clears partial payment data for security and re-prompts at recall
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task12" name="Auto-cancel timeout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Auto-cancel timeout: if suspended transaction is not recalled within configurable timeout (default 30 minutes): system auto-cancels the transaction; generates auto-cancel audit log; any loyalty points pre-earned on suspended items are reversed; Store Manager receives list of auto-cancelled transactions for review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task13" name="Maximum suspended transactions limit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Maximum suspended transactions limit: system enforces maximum of 5 suspended transactions per terminal and 20 per store at any time; if limit reached, Cashier must recall or cancel oldest suspended transaction before suspending new one
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W521_Task14" name="Store Manager terminal dashboard shows all currently suspended transactions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Store Manager terminal dashboard shows all currently suspended transactions across all store terminals: suspend ID, terminal, cashier, suspend time, item count, running total, reason code, time elapsed; color-coded (green &lt; 15 min, yellow 15–25 min, red &gt; 25 min approaching auto-cancel)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Real-time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W521_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W521_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W521_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W521_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: full audit trail and cross-terminal visibility
Owner: Cashier</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W521_Assoc17" sourceRef="W521_Annotation16" targetRef="W521_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
