    <bpmn:process id="W_W526" name="W526. POS Customer Queue Management &amp; Express Lane Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Real-time queue length exceeds configurable threshold (default: &gt; 5 customers waiting at any terminal)
Frequency: Daily during peak hours (10 AM–12 PM and 4–6 PM)
Volume: ~400 queue threshold events/day chain-wide (2 peak periods × 200 stores, though not all stores trigger every period)
Owner: Lead Cashier (queue response); Store Manager (escalation)
Participants: Lead Cashier, Store Manager, Cashiers, Customer
Source: workflow W526 — POS Customer Queue Management &amp; Express Lane Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W526_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W526_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W526_Lane2" name="Lead Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W526_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W526_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W526_Start5" name="Real-time queue length exceeds configurable threshold (default: &gt; 5 customers waiting at…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W526_Task6" name="System monitors real-time queue length per terminal: calculates queue depth…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System monitors real-time queue length per terminal: calculates queue depth from POS transaction start timestamps (time between first scan and tender completion) and estimated wait time based on current transaction speed; system also tracks queue abandonment rate (customers leaving line before reaching terminal) via entrance/exit analytics if available
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W526_Task7" name="When queue length at any terminal exceeds threshold (default 5 customers)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: When queue length at any terminal exceeds threshold (default 5 customers): system sends visual alert to Store Manager dashboard and audible alert to Lead Cashier; dashboard displays queue heat map — red (above threshold), yellow (approaching), green (normal) per terminal
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W526_Task8" name="Lead Cashier initiates queue response: opens backup terminal (if available and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lead Cashier initiates queue response: opens backup terminal (if available and staffed); assigns available cashier from float/backup pool to terminal; if no backup cashier available: Lead Cashier or Department Supervisor mans backup terminal
Responsible (R): Lead Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W526_Task9" name="Express lane activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Express lane activation (if applicable): if store has designated express lane terminal, system enables express lane criteria — maximum 10 items, no catch-weight items, no trade account pricing, no price overrides; system enforces item count at checkout; if customer exceeds 10 items: cashier offers to split into two transactions or directs to regular lane
Responsible (R): Lead Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W526_Task10" name="mPOS queue busting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: mPOS queue busting (W206): if all fixed terminals are occupied and queue persists: Lead Cashier deploys mPOS-equipped Sales Associates to process customers in queue using mobile devices; mPOS handles standard barcode-scan items, cashless payment, and e-receipts
Responsible (R): Lead Cashier / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W526_Task11" name="Lead Cashier communicates with customers in queue: provides estimated wait…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Lead Cashier communicates with customers in queue: provides estimated wait time, directs to shortest line, offers mPOS alternative; manages customer expectations during peak
Responsible (R): Lead Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W526_Task12" name="When queue subsides below threshold for 15 consecutive minutes: system sends…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: When queue subsides below threshold for 15 consecutive minutes: system sends &quot;Queue Normal&quot; notification; Lead Cashier stands down backup cashier or closes backup terminal; mPOS operators return to floor duties
Responsible (R): System / Lead Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W526_Task13" name="Weekly: Store Manager reviews queue analytics — average wait time by day and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: Store Manager reviews queue analytics — average wait time by day and hour, queue threshold trigger frequency, average queue duration, queue abandonment rate, express lane utilization rate; identifies recurring peak patterns for staffing adjustment (W34)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W526_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W526_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W526_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W526_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: Lead Cashier (queue response); Store Manager (escalation) review and approval gate
Owner: Lead Cashier (queue response); Store Manager (escalation)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W526_Assoc16" sourceRef="W526_Annotation15" targetRef="W526_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
