    <bpmn:process id="W_W535" name="W535. POS Offline Capability Scope &amp; Local Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POS terminal detects loss of WAN connectivity to ERP (network outage, ISP failure, ERP maintenance)
Frequency: Occasional — estimated 2–4 significant offline events per store per year (Philippine internet reliability); brief interruptions (&lt; 5 min) more frequent (~10–15/year per store)
Volume: Variable — worst case 8+ hours of transactions (~100–150 transactions per terminal; the chain average is ~156/terminal/day, buffered for peak hours)
Owner: Store Manager (offline operations); IT Operations (infrastructure)
Participants: Cashier, Store Manager, IT Helpdesk
Source: workflow W535 — POS Offline Capability Scope &amp; Local Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W535_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W535_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W535_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W535_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W535_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W535_Start5" name="POS terminal detects loss of WAN connectivity to ERP (network outage, ISP failure, ERP…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task6" name="POS terminal detects loss of WAN connectivity to ERP (heartbeat timeout after…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: POS terminal detects loss of WAN connectivity to ERP (heartbeat timeout after configurable interval, default 30 seconds); terminal transitions to offline mode; displays &quot;OFFLINE MODE&quot; indicator on cashier screen and customer display
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task7" name="Terminal activates local event queue; all subsequent transactions are stored as…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Terminal activates local event queue; all subsequent transactions are stored as encrypted events in local durable storage with sequence numbering; events will be replayed on reconnection per W533.10
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task8" name="Terminal activates store LAN sync (if other terminals are online via separate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Terminal activates store LAN sync (if other terminals are online via separate WAN link): broadcasts inventory deduction events to other terminals on store LAN; receives inventory deductions from other terminals; maintains consistent store-level ATP across all terminals per POS-046
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task9" name="If all terminals in store are offline (store WAN down, not just terminal)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If all terminals in store are offline (store WAN down, not just terminal): terminals continue operating independently using local data store; no terminal-to-terminal sync (each terminal has full local data); inventory overselling risk managed by per-terminal allocation from store safety stock buffer
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W535_Task10" name="Cashier continues processing transactions per standard W5B with offline…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cashier continues processing transactions per standard W5B with offline capability matrix constraints; POS terminal displays offline-appropriate prompts (e.g., &quot;Cash or card only — e-wallet unavailable during offline mode&quot;)
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W5B</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W535_Task11" name="Store Manager receives offline notification (SMS/email from IT monitoring)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Store Manager receives offline notification (SMS/email from IT monitoring); monitors offline duration; if offline exceeds 4 hours: Store Manager contacts IT Helpdesk for status update; if offline exceeds 8 hours: Store Manager activates stale-price protocol (W5G.8) — review transactions for price changes that occurred during outage
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W535_Task12" name="Quarterly: Store Manager conducts offline readiness drill — simulate WAN…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly: Store Manager conducts offline readiness drill — simulate WAN disconnection for 30 minutes during low-traffic period; verify all offline capabilities function correctly; document any issues; report to IT Operations
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): IT Operations
Duration: 30 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task13" name="WAN connectivity restored; POS terminal detects restored heartbeat; terminal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: WAN connectivity restored; POS terminal detects restored heartbeat; terminal begins uploading queued offline events to ERP message bus per W533.10
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task14" name="Terminal receives any queued price/item/promo updates that were published…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Terminal receives any queued price/item/promo updates that were published during outage; updates local data store before processing new transactions
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task15" name="ERP processes offline events: inventory deductions applied, GL entries posted…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: ERP processes offline events: inventory deductions applied, GL entries posted, loyalty points posted; system performs conflict detection per W5G (inventory conflicts, loyalty conflicts, stale pricing)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min for exception review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W535_Task16" name="Store Manager reviews and resolves any flagged exceptions per W5G; confirms…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Store Manager reviews and resolves any flagged exceptions per W5G; confirms reconciliation complete
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W5G</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W535_Task17" name="Terminal transitions to online mode; &quot;OFFLINE MODE&quot; indicator removed; all POS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Terminal transitions to online mode; &quot;OFFLINE MODE&quot; indicator removed; all POS functions restored to full capability
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W535_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W535_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W535_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W535_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: offline card store-and-forward capability; operational: receipt printing &quot;Points pending — will be posted to your account within 24 hours&quot;
Owner: Store Manager (offline operations); IT Operations (infrastructure)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W535_Assoc20" sourceRef="W535_Annotation19" targetRef="W535_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
