    <bpmn:process id="W_W539" name="W539. POS Promotional Coupon, Voucher &amp; Manufacturer Coupon Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer presents paper coupon, digital voucher, or manufacturer coupon at POS checkout
Frequency: ~140,000 coupon/voucher redemptions/month (~5% of POS transactions); spikes during sale events to ~15%
Volume: Peak: bi-monthly sales events can generate 40,000+ coupon redemptions in a single weekend
Owner: Marketing Manager (coupon design and issuance); Store Manager (redemption compliance)
Participants: Cashier (scan/validate), Customer, Store Manager (override for manual coupons), Marketing (reconciliation), Finance (manufacturer coupon reimbursement)
Source: workflow W539 — POS Promotional Coupon, Voucher &amp; Manufacturer Coupon Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W539_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W539_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W539_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W539_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W539_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W539_Start5" name="Customer presents paper coupon, digital voucher, or manufacturer coupon at POS checkout">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W539_Task6" name="Coupon scan at checkout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Coupon scan at checkout: cashier scans coupon barcode/QR code at POS; for paper coupons, cashier scans barcode; for digital vouchers, customer presents phone screen for scanning; POS validates coupon against coupon master data: (a) coupon is active and within valid date range, (b) coupon applies to items in current basket, (c) coupon usage limit not exceeded (per-coupon, per-customer, per-transaction), (d) coupon is not a duplicate (unique coupon code check), (e) coupon stacking rules allow this combination
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 sec per coupon</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W539_Task7" name="Manual coupon entry">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manual coupon entry: for coupons without scannable barcode (rare), cashier enters coupon code manually; system validates same rules; manager override required for manual entry of coupons &gt; PHP 500 value
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W539_Task8" name="Coupon application">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Coupon application: system applies coupon discount to qualifying basket items; discount shown on customer display and receipt; coupon redemption logged with unique transaction ID, cashier ID, and timestamp; coupon marked as redeemed in coupon master (prevents reuse); if coupon is manufacturer coupon, line item flagged for vendor reimbursement (FIN-019)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W539_Task9" name="Stacking and combination rules">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Stacking and combination rules: system enforces configurable stacking rules: (a) store coupon + manufacturer coupon = allowed on same item, (b) two store coupons on same item = blocked, (c) loyalty discount + coupon = lower of two applies (no double-dipping), (d) employee discount + coupon = employee discount only, (e) clearance items excluded from coupon use per W532
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W539_Task10" name="Digital voucher delivery verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Digital voucher delivery verification: for digital vouchers presented via mobile app, system validates against voucher master and confirms voucher belongs to presenting customer (loyalty ID match); prevents screenshot fraud via single-use QR with time-limited validity window
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W539_Task11" name="Coupon exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Coupon exception handling: if coupon fails validation (expired, wrong item, usage exceeded, duplicate), POS displays rejection reason; cashier communicates to customer; customer may proceed without coupon or request manager review; manager may override rejection for goodwill with reason code and documentation
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–5 min per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W539_Task12" name="End-of-day coupon reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: End-of-day coupon reconciliation: at store close (W5F), system generates coupon redemption summary: total coupons redeemed by type, total discount value, manufacturer coupon count and value for reimbursement; Store Manager reviews and confirms; summary transmitted to Finance and Marketing via event stream (W533)
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W539_Task13" name="Manufacturer coupon reimbursement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Manufacturer coupon reimbursement: Finance processes manufacturer coupon reimbursement per FIN-019 (vendor rebate management); manufacturer coupons accumulated and submitted to vendor monthly with proof-of-redemption; vendor credits BuildRight account
Responsible (R): Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Monthly batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W539_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W539_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W539_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W539_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: system-enforced rules with clear rejection messages; operational: clear documentation and photo capture at POS; operational: 3-day grace period configurable per promotion
Owner: Marketing Manager (coupon design and issuance); Store Manager (redemption compliance)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W539_Assoc16" sourceRef="W539_Annotation15" targetRef="W539_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow17" sourceRef="W539_Start5" targetRef="W539_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow18" sourceRef="W539_Task6" targetRef="W539_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow19" sourceRef="W539_Task7" targetRef="W539_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow20" sourceRef="W539_Task8" targetRef="W539_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow21" sourceRef="W539_Task9" targetRef="W539_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow22" sourceRef="W539_Task10" targetRef="W539_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow23" sourceRef="W539_Task11" targetRef="W539_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow24" sourceRef="W539_Task12" targetRef="W539_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W539_Flow25" sourceRef="W539_Task13" targetRef="W539_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
