    <bpmn:process id="W_W542" name="W542. POS Quotation &amp; Estimate Generation with Sales Conversion" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (walk-in or trade account) requests price quotation for large or project purchase at POS or trade counter/pro desk
Frequency: ~8,000 quotations/month (~0.3% of POS transactions); trade counter generates ~60% of quotations
Volume: Peak: construction season (Q1, Q4) generates 2× quotation volume
Owner: Sales Associate / Trade Counter Associate (quotation creation); Store Manager (discount authorization)
Participants: Customer, Sales Associate, Store Manager (discount approval), Trade Account Manager (for B2B quotes)
Source: workflow W542 — POS Quotation &amp; Estimate Generation with Sales Conversion</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W542_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W542_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W542_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W542_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W542_Start4" name="Customer (walk-in or trade account) requests price quotation for large or project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W542_Task5" name="Quotation request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quotation request: customer approaches POS or trade counter with list of items for quotation; Sales Associate creates new quotation in POS system; quotation captures: customer details (walk-in or account lookup), item list with quantities, requested delivery date (if applicable)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W542_Task6" name="Pricing and availability check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pricing and availability check: system auto-populates standard pricing from price master (W289); system checks real-time ATP for each item across store + DC inventory (W536.2); for items with quantity break pricing (POS-010), system shows best applicable tier; for trade accounts, system applies contracted pricing (CRM-003); out-of-stock items flagged with expected replenishment date or alternative suggestions
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W542_Task7" name="Discount application (if requested)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Discount application (if requested): if customer requests discount beyond standard pricing: Sales Associate applies discretionary discount per authorization matrix: (a) up to 5% — Sales Associate, (b) 5–10% — Department Supervisor, (c) 10–15% — Store Manager, (d) &gt; 15% — Regional Manager; discount reason code required (volume, competitor match, loyalty, project bid); system calculates margin impact for approver
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Per authorization tier
Duration: 2–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W542_Task8" name="Quotation document generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quotation document generation: system generates BIR-compliant quotation document (not an invoice — clearly labeled &quot;QUOTATION&quot;); includes: (a) unique quotation number, (b) date and validity period (configurable, default 30 days), (c) customer details, (d) item list with unit prices, quantities, and line totals, (e) applicable discounts shown separately, (f) VAT calculation, (g) total amount, (h) payment terms for trade accounts, (i) delivery terms if applicable, (j) POS terminal and associate ID; quotation printed or emailed per customer preference (per W528 e-receipt delivery)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W542_Task9" name="Quotation validity tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation validity tracking: system tracks quotation status: Open (within validity period), Expired (past validity date), Converted (sale completed), Cancelled (customer declined); daily batch flags quotations expiring within 3 days; Sales Associate proactively contacts customer for expiring quotations
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated + 5 min per follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W542_Task10" name="Quotation conversion to sale">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quotation conversion to sale: customer returns to convert quotation to sale; Sales Associate recalls quotation by quotation number; system verifies: (a) quotation is within validity period, (b) pricing still current (alerts if price changed since quotation), (c) ATP still available (alerts if stock depleted); customer confirms or adjusts quantities; system converts quotation to sales transaction (W5B) with full POS checkout
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W542_Task11" name="Quotation analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quotation analytics: monthly quotation performance report: (a) quotation count by store, (b) conversion rate by store and associate, (c) average quotation value, (d) average discount depth, (e) expired quotation analysis, (f) margin impact of quotation discounts; report feeds into W67 (store performance review) and trade sales pipeline (CRM-012)
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Monthly automated + 30 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W542_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W542_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W542_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W542_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: price-change alert at conversion with customer confirmation; operational: optional stock reservation with deposit (W545); operational: authorization matrix and monthly margin analysis
Owner: Sales Associate / Trade Counter Associate (quotation creation); Store Manager (discount authorization)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W542_Assoc14" sourceRef="W542_Annotation13" targetRef="W542_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W542_Flow15" sourceRef="W542_Start4" targetRef="W542_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W542_Flow16" sourceRef="W542_Task5" targetRef="W542_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W542_Flow17" sourceRef="W542_Task6" targetRef="W542_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W542_Flow18" sourceRef="W542_Task7" targetRef="W542_Task8" />
