    <bpmn:process id="W_W544" name="W544. POS Service Work Order Creation &amp; Scheduling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases a service (installation, assembly, custom work) at POS alongside a product
Frequency: ~14,000 service work orders/month (~0.5% of POS transactions)
Volume: Peak: construction season and holiday gift assembly (Q4) generates 2× service volume
Owner: Services Manager (scheduling and execution); Store Manager (POS-side coordination)
Participants: Sales Associate (service sale), Customer, Service Technician (execution), Services Coordinator (scheduling)
Source: workflow W544 — POS Service Work Order Creation &amp; Scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W544_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W544_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W544_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W544_Lane3" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W544_Lane4" name="Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W544_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W544_Start6" name="Customer purchases a service (installation, assembly, custom work) at POS alongside a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W544_Task7" name="Service item selection at POS">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Service item selection at POS: customer selects service alongside product purchase (e.g., ceiling fan + installation); Sales Associate scans service SKU from service catalog (non-stock item per MDM-015); system identifies service SKU type (installation, assembly, custom work, consultation); system displays service description, estimated duration, and price
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task8" name="Service scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Service scheduling: system checks technician availability calendar for the store&#x27;s service zone; presents available date/time slots to customer; customer selects preferred slot; system assigns work order to available qualified technician (skill-matched: electrical for wiring, plumbing for fixtures, etc.); for in-store services (assembly, cutting): scheduled for same-day or next available; for on-site services (installation): scheduled per customer site address and travel zone
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task9" name="Work order creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Work order creation: system generates service work order linked to POS sales transaction: (a) work order number, (b) linked sales transaction and receipt number, (c) product items requiring service, (d) service type and description, (e) customer details and site address (for on-site), (f) scheduled date/time, (g) assigned technician, (h) special instructions or customer notes; work order visible in technician&#x27;s mobile app and store services dashboard
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task10" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment processing: service fee collected at POS as part of the sales transaction (prepaid service); for large installation jobs, deposit may be collected with balance on completion per W546 (progress payment); system posts service revenue to deferred revenue (service not yet delivered); on work order completion, revenue recognized per PFRS 15 (FIN-039)
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Part of W5B checkout</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task11" name="Work order confirmation to customer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Work order confirmation to customer: system sends work order confirmation to customer via SMS/email: (a) work order number, (b) scheduled date/time, (c) assigned technician name, (d) service description, (e) store contact for rescheduling; customer can reschedule up to 24 hours before scheduled slot
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task12" name="Technician notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Technician notification: assigned technician receives work order notification in mobile app: (a) work order details, (b) product details (what to install/assemble), (c) customer site address and contact, (d) estimated duration, (e) special tools or parts needed; technician accepts or flags scheduling conflict
Responsible (R): System / Technician
Accountable (A): Services Coordinator
Duration: Automated + 5 min if conflict</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task13" name="Work order execution and completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Work order execution and completion: technician executes service per standard procedure; on completion, technician marks work order complete in mobile app with: (a) completion timestamp, (b) before/after photos (for installation), (c) customer signature on work order completion form, (d) notes on any issues or additional work needed; system triggers deferred revenue recognition for the service
Responsible (R): Technician / System
Accountable (A): Services Coordinator
Duration: Per service type</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W544_Task14" name="Post-service customer satisfaction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-service customer satisfaction: system sends post-service satisfaction survey via SMS/email (NPS); survey response linked to work order and sales transaction; low scores escalated to Services Manager per CRM-011 (feedback-to-action)
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): Services Coordinator
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W544_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W544_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W544_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W544_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: automated reminder 24 hours before, backup technician assignment, and customer rescheduling; operational: clear service description on quotation and receipt; operational: system validation of product-service compatibility at scan
Owner: Services Manager (scheduling and execution); Store Manager (POS-side coordination)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W544_Assoc17" sourceRef="W544_Annotation16" targetRef="W544_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow18" sourceRef="W544_Start6" targetRef="W544_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow19" sourceRef="W544_Task7" targetRef="W544_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow20" sourceRef="W544_Task8" targetRef="W544_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow21" sourceRef="W544_Task9" targetRef="W544_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow22" sourceRef="W544_Task10" targetRef="W544_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow23" sourceRef="W544_Task11" targetRef="W544_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow24" sourceRef="W544_Task12" targetRef="W544_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow25" sourceRef="W544_Task13" targetRef="W544_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W544_Flow26" sourceRef="W544_Task14" targetRef="W544_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W544_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W544_plane" bpmnElement="W_W544">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W544_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W544_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
