    <bpmn:process id="W_W545" name="W545. POS Special Order &amp; Customer Order Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer at POS requests an item that is out of stock at current store but available in the supply chain (DC, another store, or upcoming replenishment)
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 special orders/month (~0.1–0.15% of POS transactions; one register with the corpus canon)
Volume: Peak: during promotional stockouts, special order volume can triple
Owner: Store Manager (special order compliance); Order Fulfillment (supply chain side)
Participants: Sales Associate (order creation), Customer, Stock Associate (receiving and staging), Store Manager (exception handling)
Source: workflow W545 — POS Special Order &amp; Customer Order Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W545_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W545_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W545_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W545_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W545_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W545_Start5" name="Customer at POS requests an item that is out of stock at current store but available in…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task6" name="Special order identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Special order identification: during checkout or inquiry, customer requests item not available at store; Sales Associate checks ATP across supply chain (W536.2): (a) available at another store → offer BOPIS from that store, (b) available at DC → offer special order with DC delivery, (c) not available anywhere → check upcoming PO expected delivery date; if customer selects special order, proceed to step 2
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W545_Task7" name="Special order creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Special order creation: Sales Associate creates special order at POS: (a) customer details (name, phone, email — required for notification), (b) item(s) with quantities, (c) expected availability date (from ATP or PO ETA), (d) preferred pickup store (current store or other), (e) deposit amount (configurable: 0%, 20%, 50%, or 100% — default 20% for items ≤ PHP 10,000, 50% for items &gt; PHP 10,000)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task8" name="Deposit collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Deposit collection: system processes deposit payment via standard POS tender (W5B.7); deposit receipt printed with &quot;SPECIAL ORDER — DEPOSIT&quot; label, expected availability date, and remaining balance; deposit posted to customer deposit liability (not revenue); inventory allocated to this special order (excluded from ATP for other customers)
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task9" name="Supply chain fulfillment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Supply chain fulfillment: special order transmitted to DC or procurement via W533 event stream; DC picks and ships to designated store per standard replenishment (W4); if item requires procurement, PO created per PUR requirements with expedited flag; customer-visible tracking status updated in real-time
Responsible (R): System / DC Staff
Accountable (A): Order Fulfillment
Duration: Per W4 or PUR cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task10" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer notification: upon item arrival at store (W109 store receiving), system automatically sends customer notification: (a) SMS/email with item ready for pickup, (b) store address and operating hours, (c) remaining balance amount, (d) pickup deadline (configurable, default 14 days from notification); if customer enrolled in loyalty, notification via app as well
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W545_Task11" name="Customer pickup and balance collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer pickup and balance collection: customer arrives at store; Sales Associate recalls special order by order number or customer phone; system verifies customer identity; Stock Associate retrieves item from special order staging area; system processes balance payment (remaining amount − deposit); full sales transaction completed (W5B) with deposit applied as tender; ownership transfers, revenue recognized
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task12" name="Pickup deadline and cancellation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Pickup deadline and cancellation: if customer does not pick up within deadline (default 14 days): (a) system sends reminder at day 7 and day 12, (b) at day 14, order auto-cancelled, (c) deposit refunded per cancellation policy (configurable: full refund, less processing fee, or forfeited), (d) inventory released back to saleable ATP, (e) cancellation notification sent to customer
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated + 5 min per cancellation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W545_Task13" name="Special order analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Special order analytics: monthly special order report: (a) order count and fill rate by store, (b) average fulfillment time, (c) cancellation rate and reason, (d) deposit forfeiture revenue, (e) items most frequently special-ordered (input for assortment review W1)
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Monthly automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W545_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W545_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W545_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W545_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: realistic ETA communication and proactive delay notification; operational: 14-day deadline with auto-release and deposit policy; operational: automated deposit aging report
Owner: Store Manager (special order compliance); Order Fulfillment (supply chain side)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W545_Assoc16" sourceRef="W545_Annotation15" targetRef="W545_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W545_Flow17" sourceRef="W545_Start5" targetRef="W545_Task6" />
