    <bpmn:process id="W_W548" name="W548. POS Third-Party On-Demand Delivery Integration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer at POS requests same-day or on-demand delivery via third-party courier (Grab, Lalamove, Angkas, Borzo)
Frequency: ~14,000 on-demand deliveries/month (~0.5% of POS transactions)
Volume: Peak: weekends and rainy days generate 2× on-demand delivery demand
Owner: Store Manager (POS-side coordination); Logistics (3PL relationship management per W62B)
Participants: Cashier (order creation), Customer, On-Demand Courier, Stock Associate (staging)
Source: workflow W548 — POS Third-Party On-Demand Delivery Integration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W548_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W548_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W548_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W548_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W548_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W548_Lane5" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W548_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W548_Start7" name="Customer at POS requests same-day or on-demand delivery via third-party courier (Grab…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W548_Task8" name="On-demand delivery request at POS">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: On-demand delivery request at POS: at checkout, customer requests delivery instead of carry-out; cashier selects &quot;On-Demand Delivery&quot; option in POS; system prompts for delivery address (customer input or loyalty profile address); system displays delivery fee estimate based on distance zone; customer confirms delivery
Responsible (R): Cashier / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W548_Task9" name="Courier platform API call">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Courier platform API call: POS system (or store associate via integrated dispatch portal) sends delivery request to configured on-demand courier platform API: (a) pickup location (store address + contact), (b) delivery address, (c) item description and estimated weight, (d) required vehicle type (motorcycle for small items, car/SUV for medium, van/truck for bulky), (e) special instructions (fragile, heavy lifting); platform confirms driver assignment and ETA
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W548_Task10" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Payment processing: customer pays for merchandise via standard POS tender (W5B.7); delivery fee added as separate line item on receipt; delivery fee collected by BuildRight and remitted to courier platform (or customer pays courier directly — configurable per platform); sale completes and inventory deducted
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Part of W5B checkout</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W548_Task11" name="Item staging and handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Item staging and handoff: Stock Associate stages items at designated pickup area; courier arrives per platform ETA; Stock Associate verifies courier identity (platform-provided name, vehicle, and OTP from customer); Stock Associate hands items to courier; system logs handoff timestamp and courier details
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Courier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W548_Task12" name="Delivery tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Delivery tracking: customer receives real-time delivery tracking via platform app; BuildRight system receives delivery status updates via platform API webhook: (a) courier en route, (b) courier arrived at customer, (c) delivery completed with proof-of-delivery photo; delivery status visible in customer&#x27;s BuildRight order history
Responsible (R): System / Courier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W548_Task13" name="Delivery exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Delivery exception handling: if delivery fails (customer not available, wrong address, item damaged in transit): (a) platform attempts redelivery or returns items to store, (b) Stock Associate receives returned items and restocks, (c) delivery fee refund processed per platform policy, (d) merchandise refund per standard return policy (W12) if customer requests; Store Manager reviews exception
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W548_Task14" name="Delivery settlement reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Delivery settlement reconciliation: weekly, Finance reconciles on-demand delivery fees: (a) delivery fees collected from customers vs. fees charged by courier platforms, (b) platform commission reconciliation, (c) failed delivery refunds, (d) GL posting for delivery fee revenue and courier expense; settlement report generated per platform
Responsible (R): Finance / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Weekly batch ~2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W548_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W548_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W548_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W548_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: multi-platform integration (Grab + Lalamove + Angkas) for redundancy; operational: proper packaging at staging, delivery insurance via platform, and damage claim process; operational: dynamic fee calculation based on distance and weight
Owner: Store Manager (POS-side coordination); Logistics (3PL relationship management per W62B)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W548_Assoc17" sourceRef="W548_Annotation16" targetRef="W548_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
