    <bpmn:process id="W_W552" name="W552. POS Donation &amp; Charity Round-Up Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POS system prompts for donation round-up after tender selection; customer opts in
Frequency: ~140,000 donation transactions/month (~5% of POS transactions opt in)
Volume: Average donation: ~PHP 7 (round-up from PHP 1,793 to PHP 1,800); total ~PHP 980K/month
Owner: Corporate Communications (charity partnerships); Store Manager (POS compliance)
Participants: Cashier (prompting), Customer, Charity Partner, Finance (donation remittance)
Source: workflow W552 — POS Donation &amp; Charity Round-Up Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W552_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W552_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W552_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W552_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W552_Lane4" name="Corp Communications">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W552_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W552_Start6" name="POS system prompts for donation round-up after tender selection; customer opts in">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task7" name="Donation prompt at checkout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Donation prompt at checkout: after tender is processed (W5B.7) and change is calculated, system displays donation prompt on customer-facing screen: &quot;Round up to PHP [next even amount] for [Charity Name]? Your donation: PHP [round-up amount]&quot;; customer taps &quot;Yes&quot; or &quot;No Thanks&quot; on customer-facing display; if customer-facing display not available, cashier verbally prompts
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task8" name="Donation amount options">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Donation amount options: customer selects from: (a) round-up (default — rounds to nearest PHP 10 or PHP 100), (b) fixed amount buttons (PHP 10, PHP 25, PHP 50, PHP 100), (c) custom amount; selected donation added as separate line item on receipt labeled &quot;Donation — [Charity Name]&quot;
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task9" name="Donation receipt and documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Donation receipt and documentation: receipt prints donation line item with: (a) charity name and registration number, (b) donation amount, (c) BuildRight corporate donation reference; donation is NOT tax-deductible to customer (no BIR tax credit); for customer records, receipt serves as proof of donation; system does not charge VAT on donation amount
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Part of receipt printing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task10" name="Fund segregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fund segregation: system posts donation amount to segregated charity liability account (not revenue); donations accumulated per charity partner per store per period; donations excluded from store revenue and sales metrics (W67 store performance) to prevent donation-inflated revenue reporting
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W552_Task11" name="Charity remittance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Charity remittance: monthly (or per campaign end), Finance remits accumulated donations to charity partner: (a) total donation amount per charity, (b) store-level breakdown, (c) transaction count, (d) official donation receipt from charity for BuildRight records; remittance per BIR donation documentation requirements (corporate donor)
Responsible (R): Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Monthly batch ~4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task12" name="Campaign management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Campaign management: Corporate Communications configures donation campaigns: (a) active charity partner(s), (b) campaign start/end dates, (c) round-up rules, (d) fixed amount options, (e) campaign messaging on customer display; multiple campaigns can be active simultaneously (one per region or cause); campaign pushed to POS terminals via W533 price/content push mechanism
Responsible (R): Corp Communications / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per campaign setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W552_Task13" name="Donation analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Donation analytics: weekly donation dashboard: (a) total donations by charity and store, (b) opt-in rate (% of transactions with donation), (c) average donation amount, (d) campaign performance vs. target; monthly donation report for ESG reporting (GOV-008) and corporate communications
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W552_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W552_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W552_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W552_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: prompt only once per transaction, easy &quot;No Thanks&quot; option, and configurable prompt frequency (e.g., skip every other transaction for same customer); operational: cashier training (W518) and analytics visibility; operational: system-enforced GL routing for donation line items
Owner: Corporate Communications (charity partnerships); Store Manager (POS compliance)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W552_Assoc16" sourceRef="W552_Annotation15" targetRef="W552_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow17" sourceRef="W552_Start6" targetRef="W552_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow18" sourceRef="W552_Task7" targetRef="W552_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow19" sourceRef="W552_Task8" targetRef="W552_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow20" sourceRef="W552_Task9" targetRef="W552_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow21" sourceRef="W552_Task10" targetRef="W552_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow22" sourceRef="W552_Task11" targetRef="W552_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow23" sourceRef="W552_Task12" targetRef="W552_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W552_Flow24" sourceRef="W552_Task13" targetRef="W552_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
