    <bpmn:process id="W_W1494" name="W1494. POS Customer Project Receipt, Multi-Store Purchase Aggregation &amp; Tax Credit Certificate Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests an aggregated receipt or tax credit certificate (TCC) for project purchases made across multiple BuildRight stores over a period of time
Frequency: ~10–20 requests per store per month; higher for stores near commercial zones and government project offices
Volume: ~10,000–20,000 project receipt requests/month chain-wide
Owner: CSR
Participants: Customer, CSR, Store Manager, Tax Compliance Associate (HQ)
Source: workflow W1494 — POS Customer Project Receipt, Multi-Store Purchase Aggregation &amp; Tax Credit Certificate Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1494_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1494_Lane1" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1494_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1494_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1494_Start4" name="Customer requests an aggregated receipt or tax credit certificate (TCC) for project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1494_Task5" name="Project receipt request intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project receipt request intake: Customer requests project receipt at service counter or via the trade portal: (a) customer provides project reference number (assigned at first project-related purchase or registered in trade account portal); (b) system looks up all transactions linked to the project reference across all BuildRight stores; (c) customer specifies: (i) date range; (ii) store filter (all stores or specific stores); (iii) receipt format: summary or detailed (line-item); (iv) VAT breakdown required: yes/no
Responsible (R): CSR / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1494_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1494_Task6" name="Multi-store transaction aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Multi-store transaction aggregation: (a) system queries transaction database across all 200 stores for the given project reference and date range; (b) transactions matched by: (i) project reference number linked at point of sale; (ii) trade account number; (iii) loyalty card number as fallback; (c) system consolidates: (i) all individual receipt numbers, dates, store locations; (ii) total amount per VAT category (VATable, VAT-exempt, zero-rated); (iii) total VAT amount; (iv) total amount paid by payment method; (d) aggregation completes within 30 seconds for typical project (50–200 transactions); (e) CSR previews consolidated report on screen for customer verification
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1494_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1494_Task7" name="Tax credit certificate generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Tax credit certificate generation (if requested): (a) for customers eligible for TCC (registered VAT taxpayer with valid TIN): (b) system generates BIR-compliant TCC format: (i) seller TIN and registered name; (ii) buyer TIN and registered name/address; (iii) total sales amount and VAT amount; (iv) individual invoice numbers covered; (v) certification period; (c) TCC digitally signed by authorized BuildRight signatory (Tax Compliance Associate or CFO for amounts &gt; PHP 1M); (d) TCC printed on BIR-authorized security paper (if physical copy requested) or sent as digitally signed PDF
Responsible (R): CSR / Tax Compliance Associate
Accountable (A): CFO (for amounts &gt; PHP 1M)
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1494_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1494_Task8" name="Project receipt issuance &amp; archival">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Project receipt issuance &amp; archival: (a) final project receipt reviewed by CSR and customer; (b) any discrepancies resolved (missing transactions, duplicate entries, wrong project assignment); (c) project receipt generated as PDF with unique document control number; (d) original individual POS receipts remain valid; project receipt serves as supplementary summary document; (e) project receipt archived in system for 10-year BIR retention requirement; (f) customer receives: printed copy (if requested), PDF via email, and portal download link
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1494_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1494_Task9" name="Project receipt audit trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Project receipt audit trail: (a) system maintains full audit trail: which individual receipts are included, any manual adjustments, who authorized the aggregation; (b) BIR audit support: Tax Compliance Associate can regenerate any project receipt from archive and provide supporting individual receipts; (c) if BIR challenges the TCC: Tax Compliance Associate provides electronic transaction logs as corroboration
Responsible (R): System / Tax Compliance Associate
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per audit request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1494_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1494_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1494_End10" name="Complete">
