    <bpmn:process id="W_W5547" name="W5547. Payment-Network &amp; Acquirer Outage Response (Card Scheme / Acquirer Downtime)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Chain-wide or regional inability to authorize or settle card transactions during trading hours — a card-scheme outage (Visa/Mastercard/JCB), an acquiring-bank processor platform failure, or loss of connectivity between the POS estate and the acquirer exceeding 15 minutes at peak or 60 minutes off-peak
Frequency: ~2–4 events/yr chain-wide (industry reality; most resolve within 1 hour; the rare multi-hour or multi-day processor failure is the tail case this protocol covers)
Volume: 1 event × 200 stores × the ~36% card tender share of 2.8M monthly POS transactions (≈ 33,000 card transactions/day chain-wide) × peak-hour lost-basket exposure per the PHP 840K/day per-store revenue canon
Owner: Head of Customer Service (chain-wide protocol); Store Manager (site execution)
Participants: Store Managers &amp; Front-End Supervisors, IT Service Desk (connectivity triage vs acquirer-side), acquirer relationship manager, Loss Prevention (outage-window fraud watch), Finance (settlement catch-up per W537/W3701), Marketing/Communications (customer messaging), Ecommerce lead (if online checkout affected)
Source: workflow W5547 — Payment-Network &amp; Acquirer Outage Response (Card Scheme / Acquirer Downtime)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5547_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane1" name="IT Service Desk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane2" name="Head of Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane3" name="Store Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane4" name="Front-End">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane5" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5547_Lane6" name="Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5547_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5547_Start8" name="Chain-wide or regional inability to authorize or settle card transactions during trading…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task9" name="Outage detection &amp; classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Outage detection &amp; classification: acquirer heartbeat/terminal dashboard or store reports trigger the event; classify: scheme-side (all issuers affected) vs acquirer-processor side vs BuildRight connectivity (the last routes to W535/W1531 mechanics instead); confirm scope (chain/regional/single store) and expected duration from the acquirer&#x27;s status line
Responsible (R): IT Service Desk / Head of Customer Service
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Service
Duration: &lt; 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task10" name="Chain-wide tender-degradation notice">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chain-wide tender-degradation notice: push the standard protocol to all affected stores — POS messaging &quot;card payments temporarily unavailable — cash, GCash/Maya and bank transfer accepted&quot;; queue management (open lanes, floor staff to queues); high-basket customers offered item-hold or invoice-now-pay-later only per existing store-credit policy (never improvised)
Responsible (R): Head of Customer Service / Store Managers
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: &lt; 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task11" name="Alternative-tender surge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Alternative-tender surge: e-wallet QR signage deployed at lanes; cash handling surge per W541-class cash-office rhythm; manual imprint/fallback authorization only where and as the acquirer instructs (contract-defined); save-the-sale desk for large baskets with delivery (delivery-on-payment options per W5D)
Responsible (R): Store Managers / Front-End
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Service
Duration: During outage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task12" name="Offline authorization discipline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Offline authorization discipline: where the acquirer permits offline floor limits during outages, enforce the configured caps and the manual-referral phone line; LP watches the window for stolen-card abuse of offline authorization; every offline transaction logged for post-recovery settlement
Responsible (R): Front-End / LP
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: During outage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task13" name="Recovery &amp; settlement catch-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Recovery &amp; settlement catch-up: on acquirer all-clear, terminals resettle pending batches; Finance runs the W537 settlement reconciliation with a duplicate-charge sweep (authorizations during the outage that were retried); customer-facing duplicate concerns handled by Customer Service with receipts
Responsible (R): IT / Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task14" name="Customer follow-through">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer follow-through: for customers who saw declines that later authorized — proactive receipt/charge clarifications; chargeback-prevention evidence (receipts, CCTV per W471 rules) retained for the dispute window; goodwill per policy where a wrong decline caused hardship
Responsible (R): Customer Service / LP
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Service
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5547_Task15" name="Post-mortem &amp; acquirer accountability">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-mortem &amp; acquirer accountability: RCA with the acquirer/processor; SLA-credit claims per contract; the event and response gaps feed the tender-resilience roadmap (secondary acquirer evaluation, terminal multi-acquirer failover)
Responsible (R): Head of Customer Service / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5547_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5547_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5547_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5547_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).); CTL-184 (ensure POS settlement &amp; tender reconciliation completeness.) | - operational: manual imprint/fallback authorization only per acquirer instruction and configured floor limits — never improvised at store level | - operational: every outage event closes with the W537 settlement reconciliation signed off, including the duplicate-charge sweep result
Owner: Head of Customer Service (chain-wide protocol); Store Manager (site execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5547_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5547_Annotation17" targetRef="W5547_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
