    <bpmn:process id="W_W5564" name="W5564. Mobile-Wallet Platform Outage Response (E-Wallet Tender Downtime)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A mobile-wallet provider platform failure (GCash/Maya class) disabling e-wallet tender — QR scan-to-pay and NFC wallet authorization — chain-wide during trading hours while card and cash rails keep working; distinct from W5547&#x27;s card-scheme/acquirer class (different rail, counterparty and settlement) and from W535&#x27;s store-connectivity class (the store&#x27;s link is up; the wallet provider is down)
Frequency: ~2–4 degradation/outage events per year across the wallet providers (app-wide incidents are recurring industry reality); most resolve within 1–2 hours, the rare multi-hour event is the tail case this protocol covers
Volume: 1 event × 200 stores × the e-wallet tender share (~15% of 2.8M monthly POS transactions ≈ ~14,000 wallet transactions/day chain-wide) × the alternative-tender surge at peak
Owner: Head of Customer Service (chain-wide tender protocol); Store Manager (site execution)
Participants: Cashier, Front-End Supervisor, IT Service Desk (rail diagnosis), wallet-provider relationship manager, Loss Prevention (outage-window fraud watch), Finance (wallet-settlement catch-up), Ecommerce lead (checkout wallet options), Marketing/Communications (customer messaging)
Source: workflow W5564 — Mobile-Wallet Platform Outage Response (E-Wallet Tender Downtime)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5564_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane1" name="IT Service Desk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane2" name="Head of Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane4" name="Loss Prevention">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane5" name="Ecommerce lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5564_Lane6" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5564_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5564_Start8" name="A mobile-wallet provider platform failure (GCash/Maya class) disabling e-wallet tender —…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task9" name="Rail diagnosis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Rail diagnosis: distinguish provider outage (multiple stores + provider status channels) vs store connectivity (W535) vs acquirer path (W5547); engage the provider relationship manager for confirmation and ETA
Responsible (R): IT Service Desk
Accountable (A): IT Operations
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task10" name="Tender-policy directive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tender-policy directive: disable wallet tender via the POS tender-type flag (a directive, never ad-hoc cashier rejections); script to all crews; alternative-tender surge per the W5547 law
Responsible (R): Head of Customer Service
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Service
Duration: Same window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task11" name="Customer handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer handling: signage and scripts at entrances and lanes; queued wallet-payers offered card/cash; no manual receipts or IOUs for wallet payments (the wallet may retry and double-charge on recovery)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Same window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task12" name="Fraud watch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fraud watch: outage windows breed &quot;wallet error&quot; refund scams, phished-OTP social engineering and double-scan attempts; LP watch per W605/W3699 signals
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: Same window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task13" name="Ecommerce fallback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Ecommerce fallback: wallet options disabled at checkout; card/COD fallback messaging per W659
Responsible (R): Ecommerce lead
Accountable (A): Digital Commerce GM
Duration: Same window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task14" name="Recovery &amp; settlement catch-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Recovery &amp; settlement catch-up: re-enable tender after provider confirmation; sweep stranded wallet authorizations against the provider&#x27;s T+1 settlement statement so no authorized payment is lost or double-charged
Responsible (R): Finance / IT
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 days post-recovery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5564_Task15" name="After-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: After-action: provider SLA/penalty posture per contract; outage duration and tender-shift capture feeding the tender-mix model
Responsible (R): Finance / Head of Customer Service
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5564_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5564_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5564_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5564_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-263 (ensure controlled execution — Transaction Processing (PA-08.1).) | - operational: wallet tender is disabled and restored only by directive flag with audit trail; stranded authorizations reconciled against the provider statement before the event is closed; outage-window refund exceptions routed to LP review
Owner: Head of Customer Service (chain-wide tender protocol); Store Manager (site execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
